{# English rule summaries for the AGENTS.md ethics appendix (agents_md_language == 'en').

   kanon's sections are Japanese-only, and daimonion renders them verbatim
   into the marker block. Until kanon ships English text (memo KN-1), this
   partial carries an English translation of each section's title and
   `要約` (rule summary) lines, snapshot of kanon 2321063 -- the revision
   the pinned daimonion (`daimonion_spec`) vendors. Rows mirror kanon's
   `status=active`, `placement: agents_md` sections (draft sections never
   reach the block) in sections/MANIFEST.yml order; `when` is the
   manifest's any-of list (`always` applies to every project). Re-translate a row whenever
   bumping `daimonion_spec` changes the vendored section's summary, and
   delete this partial once daimonion renders English itself.

   The selection replays daimonion's `Section.applies` over the same derived
   condition set `.daimonion.yml` carries (`_shared/daimonion-when.jinja`),
   so the summaries name exactly the sections the block below holds.
   tests/test_daimonion_config.py pins both the rows and the selection
   against the vendored kanon. -#}
{% import "_shared/daimonion-when.jinja" as dw with context -%}
{% set when_set = ['always'] -%}
{% for line in dw.daimonion_when().splitlines() if line.strip() -%}
{% set _ = when_set.append(line.split()[1]) -%}
{% endfor -%}
{% set sections = [
    {'id': 'baseline-copyright-ai', 'when': ['cli', 'data_science'],
     'title': 'AI and copyright: fetching, training and RAG code must not break the non-enjoyment exception',
     'rules': ['do not circumvent robots.txt or other crawl-refusal measures',
               'do not design RAG that retrieves and re-emits the expression itself; extract facts and concepts only',
               'do not overfit or fine-tune on a specific body of works in order to imitate it']},
    {'id': 'baseline-license-drift', 'when': ['always'],
     'title': "License drift: track dependencies' current licenses and keep BSL/SSPL out",
     'rules': ['check the current license when adding a dependency and match it against the allowlist',
               'never pull in source-available licenses (BSL, SSPL, ...) unchecked',
               'route fork migrations (Terraform to OpenTofu, ...) through the legitimate successor']},
    {'id': 'baseline-personal-data', 'when': ['personal_data', 'face_recognition', 'medtech'],
     'title': 'Personal data: minimise before collecting, build the deletion path first',
     'rules': ['ask "is this needed?" before collecting, and keep the defaults minimal',
               'design deletion and correction paths from the start (retrofitting is expensive)',
               'know what leaves the process (Sentry, cloud, external APIs) and reduce it before it leaves']},
    {'id': 'baseline-pki-chain', 'when': ['embedded', 'cli', 'web_api'],
     'title': 'PKI chain changes: never hard-code intermediate certificates or issuance chains',
     'rules': ['do not bundle or pin intermediate certificates or issuance chains',
               'verify against the OS/system trust store and keep a way to update it',
               'when pinning, pin a public-key set plus backup keys, never a single key']},
    {'id': 'baseline-pqc-fips', 'when': ['library', 'cli', 'web_api'],
     'title': 'PQC standards: new cryptographic choices use ML-KEM/ML-DSA, in hybrid mode',
     'rules': ['use the standard names (ML-KEM / ML-DSA / SLH-DSA), not submission names such as Kyber, in new code',
               'key exchange is ML-KEM; signatures default to ML-DSA with SLH-DSA as the conservative alternative; do not mix the roles',
               'migrate in hybrid mode (X25519MLKEM768, ...) and adopt no classical-only scheme anew']},
    {'id': 'domain-contest-rules', 'when': ['oj_code'],
     'title': "Contest rules: AI use differs per contest, and submissions are the participant's responsibility",
     'rules': ['AI use is allowed or not per contest and period, so check the current rules before generating or submitting',
               'treat unclear rules as a ban',
               "submissions are the participant's own responsibility; multiple accounts and rating manipulation are banned on every judge"]},
    {'id': 'domain-face-recognition', 'when': ['face_recognition'],
     'title': 'Face recognition: biometric identification is an exception; confirm the use is lawful first',
     'rules': ['confirm the use is lawful before implementing; for a prohibited use, write no code',
               'keep biometric templates non-reversible, with consent and deletion paths',
               'measure accuracy per demographic group; do not default to a single threshold']},
    {'id': 'domain-llm-appsec', 'when': ['mcp'],
     'title': 'LLM apps and MCP: least privilege, human approval and output validation by default',
     'rules': ['restrict tool permissions to a minimal allowlisted CRUD set',
               'always insert a human approval step before destructive or irreversible operations',
               'validate LLM output structurally before acting on it; never pass it straight to a shell']},
    {'id': 'domain-ml-bias', 'when': ['data_science', 'kaggle'],
     'title': 'ML bias: build per-group evaluation, explainability and human review into evaluation',
     'rules': ['always report per-group performance, not just average accuracy',
               'dropping a protected attribute does not by itself remove discrimination (handle proxies)',
               'require human review for decisions that affect life opportunities']},
    {'id': 'domain-scraping-law', 'when': ['scraping'],
     'title': 'Scraping legality: check rights, contracts and personal data before fetching',
     'rules': ["settle whether fetching is allowed per site, from its terms and robots.txt, first",
               'even public data can infringe other rights when a substantial part of a database is extracted or its expression redistributed',
               'personal data is regulated both when fetched and when processed']},
    {'id': 'region-eu-cra', 'when': ['commercial'],
     'title': 'EU CRA: vulnerability reporting and SBOMs are no longer optional for commercial software',
     'rules': ['report an actively exploited vulnerability within 24 hours of becoming aware of it',
               'produce an SBOM and be able to explain where every dependency comes from',
               'state the support period and ship security updates throughout it']},
    {'id': 'sector-samd-regulatory', 'when': ['medtech'],
     'title': 'Medical SaMD: continuous learning stays within the approved change limits, and humans make the call',
     'rules': ['never swap a production model outside the approved change plan (PCCP / IDATEN, ...)',
               'default to a structure where a human (a physician, ...) makes the final decision',
               'build performance-drift monitoring and post-market surveillance into the initial design']},
] -%}
### Rule summaries (English)

English summaries of the kanon sections this project's `.daimonion.yml`
selects. The full sections in the marker block below (facts, prohibited
patterns, regex triggers) are written in Japanese; these summaries translate
their rule lines. Not legal advice.

{% set chosen = [] -%}
{% for s in sections -%}
{% for w in s.when if w in when_set -%}
{% if s not in chosen %}{% set _ = chosen.append(s) %}{% endif -%}
{% endfor -%}
{% endfor -%}
{% for s in chosen -%}
- **{{ s.title }}** (`{{ s.id }}`): (1) {{ s.rules[0] }}; (2) {{ s.rules[1] }}; (3) {{ s.rules[2] }}.
{% endfor -%}
